.\" Manpage for NixOS-bunker operator tools (host).
.TH BUNKER 1 "July 2026" "nixos-bunker" "NixOS-bunker Manual"
.SH NAME
bunker \- NixOS-bunker host operator overview (Qubes-like zones)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bunker-zones
.br
.B bunker-deniable
.br
.B bunker-panic-ui
.br
.B bunker-zone
.RI [ list | add | set | rm | \&.\&.\&. ]
.br
.B bunker-broker
.br
.B bunker-zone-start
.IR zone | all
.br
.B bunker-term
.I zone
.br
.B bunker-clip
.RI [ send | copy | clear ]
.br
.B bunker-usb-attach
.I zone vid:pid
.br
.B man bunker
.SH DESCRIPTION
NixOS-bunker is a hardened NixOS host with apps in microVM
.B zones
(AppVMs / Disposables / Templates), plus
.B netVM
and
.B usbVM
brokers. The host GNOME session is intentionally thin: launchers, terminal,
settings, and emergency disk/backup tools for when VMs are unavailable.
.PP
Daily apps belong in zones. Do not install browsers or mail on the host.
.PP
Zone CRUD belongs in
.B zones.json
via
.B bunker-zones
(ratatui) or
.BR bunker-zone
(CLI). Hand-editing
.I zones.json
is fine. Hand-editing Nix modules for per-zone add/remove is
.B discouraged .
.PP
Entire VMs may be
.B deniable
(Shufflecake layers): see
.B bunker-deniable
and
.IR docs/deniable.md .
.B bunker-panic-ui
destroys panic-flagged deniable keys only (not public decoys / host LUKS).
.SH HOST VS ZONES
.TP
.B Host (this machine)
GNOME shell, zone launchers, bunker-* CLI, disk repair, backups of the host
itself. Users: bunker (daily), admin (wheel / nixos-rebuild).
.TP
.B AppVM / Disposable
Defined in
.IR config/zones.json
(CRUD via
.B bunker-zones
/
.BR bunker-zone ).
Templates live in
.IR templates/*.nix .
.TP
.B Deniable VM
.IR config/deniable-zones.json
— whole microVMs on Shufflecake layers; shown only when unlocked.
.TP
.B Service
net · netvm, usb · usbvm, zones · service, deniable · service, panic · service,
defaults · service, killswitch, help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B bunker-zones
Ratatui CRUD for AppVMs / Disposables (preferred UX). Launcher:
.BR "zones · service" .
.TP
.B bunker-deniable
Hide/show whole VMs via Shufflecake layers. Launcher:
.BR "deniable · service" .
.TP
.B bunker-panic-ui
Panic button (nuclear icon): wipe panic-flagged deniable keys + RAM wipe.
Launcher:
.BR "panic · service" .
.TP
.B bunker-zone
CLI CRUD zones, apps, USB defaults, colors, templates.
.TP
.B bunker-broker
Ratatui net/usb/voice/metadata defaults (keys 1–4; mat2 when metadata=on).
Launcher:
.BR "defaults · service" .
.TP
.B bunker-zone-start
Start microVM(s); attaches zone USB defaults.
.TP
.B bunker-term
Colored SSH shell into a zone (or net/usb).
.TP
.B bunker-clip send|copy|clear
Mediated clipboard. Host clip kept on send; zone clip clears after TTL
(default 30s; see
.IR /etc/bunker/clipboard.conf ).
.TP
.B bunker-usb-attach / bunker-usb-detach
usbVM broker (1→many) via usbip.
.TP
.B bunker-killswitch
Block app-guest WAN; allow vm-net only.
.TP
.B bunker-wipe
Wipe disposable zone data.
.TP
.B bunker-test-isolation
Policy greps; optional
.B --live
probes.
.TP
.B bunker-first-boot / bunker-update
First-boot checklist / pull+rebuild helper.
.SH EMERGENCY HOST TOOLS
When locked out of VMs, use host menu / PATH:
.BR gnome-disks ,
.BR gparted ,
.BR nautilus ,
.BR baobab ,
.BR gnome-text-editor ,
.BR gnome-logs ,
plus CLI
.BR cryptsetup ,
.BR parted ,
.BR smartctl ,
.BR nvme ,
.BR ddrescue ,
.BR testdisk ,
.BR rsync ,
.BR borg ,
.BR mat2
/
.BR bunker-mat
(EXIF strip).
Prefer
.B admin
(sudo) for destructive disk work.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bunker/zones.json
Installed zone registry (SoT is the flake checkout).
.TP
.I /etc/bunker/clipboard.conf
Clipboard TTL (hackable).
.TP
.I /etc/bunker/MANUAL
Plain-text copy of this overview (no man required).
.TP
.I /etc/bunker/qube-model
Short Qubes-like model reminder.
